# interplay_memlive_shared_table_held: Two tasks over one page table and one object list (task 2's task     root names task 1's table root and task 1's list, as     memory_gap_shared_tables does), so both see the same VAs: task 2's     first read of buffers A and B waits on the gate while the guest points     the shared leaves of A's and B's pages at other pages, and task 1 then     reads both. Task 1's A, made before the rewrite, keeps its old page;     its B, first made after, is made over the new one (task 1 runs on the worker FIFO, child 2: the root FIFO is held). Released, task 2     makes its own A and B over the rewritten leaves: both of its reads show     the new pages (objects are a task's own; the table is shared).
